Shows what an eero mesh Wi-Fi network is doing, from the OPNsense GUI: each
eero unit (online, model, backhaul, mesh quality, clients, uptime) with a page
for its clients, radios, ports and history; every Wi-Fi client (which unit it
is on, band and channel, signal, connection quality) with its moves between
units; and the network's settings and health, including which unit eero
treats as primary. Units can be renamed from the GUI; nothing else is changed
at eero.

A small service polls eero's cloud API (the one the eero app uses) at a
gentle, rate-limited pace and keeps the results in SQLite; the GUI only
reads that copy. It records client moves and unit status changes, kept for
7 days unless changed. Log in once from the GUI with the code eero sends you.

With os-loupe installed, clients show Loupe's names, device types, icons and
makers.

Plugin Changelog
================

1.0

* Unit page: the clients on it now, its radios (channel, width, clients,
  transmit power), ports (link speed, uplink, LLDP neighbours), firmware,
  power source and serial, and its status changes (offline, back online,
  became primary)
* Rename a unit from the GUI (the pencil by its name); a privilege of its own,
  "eero: rename units"
* Client page: time on each unit and the client's moves; Recent moves lists
  the latest moves across all clients
* Clients show band and channel and eero's connection quality instead of the
  link rate
* Overview tab (was Network), with the primary unit
* Keep history setting: days of moves and status changes to keep (default 7)
* With os-loupe: Loupe's names (after names set in the eero app), types, icons
  and makers
* Host names that are raw bytes (some devices send them over DHCP) count as no
  name

0.1

* Initial release
